1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:00,712
Part six.

2
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:02,038
Three firebreaks.

3
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:03,525
Remember the wildfire?

4
00:00:03,938 --> 00:00:05,338
You can't stop every spark.

5
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:07,012
But you can build firebreaks.

6
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:08,400
And Pape names three.

7
00:00:08,862 --> 00:00:09,525
Firebreak one.

8
00:00:09,938 --> 00:00:11,250
Every member of Congress,

9
00:00:11,625 --> 00:00:12,725
old and newly elected,

10
00:00:13,025 --> 00:00:13,962
says one thing:

11
00:00:14,438 --> 00:00:17,050
no escalation in Iran until the new Congress

12
00:00:17,062 --> 00:00:17,588
is seated,

13
00:00:17,975 --> 00:00:19,575
unless Iran strikes first.

14
00:00:20,038 --> 00:00:20,737
Firebreak two.

15
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,200
Every governor and mayor calls for a two

16
00:00:23,212 --> 00:00:25,538
month pause on federally armed agents in their

17
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:27,325
cities, unless they ask for them.

18
00:00:27,738 --> 00:00:29,838
Take the key sparks off the table while

19
00:00:29,850 --> 00:00:30,738
votes are counted.

20
00:00:31,212 --> 00:00:32,025
Firebreak three.

21
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:34,288
The countries acting as mediators,

22
00:00:34,462 --> 00:00:36,488
Pakistan, Qatar and India,

23
00:00:36,788 --> 00:00:38,700
call on everyone to do one thing:

24
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:40,262
hands off civilians.

25
00:00:40,675 --> 00:00:43,838
No direct targeting of civilian infrastructure or homes.

26
00:00:44,262 --> 00:00:45,500
So should you stockpile water?

27
00:00:45,925 --> 00:00:46,762
Pape says he isn't.

28
00:00:47,175 --> 00:00:48,762
On day one you drink one bottle.

29
00:00:49,188 --> 00:00:50,113
By day three you're out.

30
00:00:50,525 --> 00:00:51,850
And the attacks can come again.

31
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,462
Three days of supplies doesn't buy real time.

32
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:55,762
The firebreaks do.

33
00:00:56,175 --> 00:00:57,775
So what can an ordinary person do?

34
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:58,850
Pape says:

35
00:00:59,288 --> 00:01:02,025
email, text, or call your political leaders,

36
00:01:02,250 --> 00:01:03,012
whoever they are,

37
00:01:03,288 --> 00:01:05,825
and ask them to adopt those three firebreaks.

38
00:01:06,238 --> 00:01:08,762
Otherwise, we're just letting events control us.

39
00:01:09,175 --> 00:01:11,512
And he believes conversations like this one matter.

40
00:01:11,925 --> 00:01:13,712
After his last appearance on the show,

41
00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:16,525
he says, momentum for a major strike on

42
00:01:16,538 --> 00:01:18,225
Iran's drone network faded,

43
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,738
and he credits public attention as one of

44
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:21,413
the reasons.

45
00:01:21,825 --> 00:01:23,038
Asked if he's a pessimist,

46
00:01:23,275 --> 00:01:24,425
Pape says the opposite.

47
00:01:24,862 --> 00:01:26,125
He lays out the dark road,

48
00:01:26,512 --> 00:01:28,188
not because he wants the doom loop,

49
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,150
but because he wants us to choose a

50
00:01:30,162 --> 00:01:30,762
better one.

51
00:01:31,188 --> 00:01:32,675
This was ninety minutes in ten.

52
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,900
The full conversation goes deeper,

53
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:36,388
into Putin's maps,

54
00:01:36,588 --> 00:01:37,675
the Insurrection Act,

55
00:01:37,938 --> 00:01:38,875
and the White House.

